   01-04, 2004},
Organization = {IFU IMK},
Abstract = {The present study analyses the influence of traffic-produced turbulence
   (TPT) on CO concentration using full-scale measurements obtained in
   Gottinger Strasse (Hannover, Germany). Cases with airflow within +/-
   11.25 degrees from the direction perpendicular to the street axis were
   used. The values C = Ci-Cb (Ci is concentration measured inside the
   street canyon and Cb is the background concentration) were plotted
   against ambient wind speed (U) for different traffic volumes. For
   windward conditions, the data verified the form C alpha U-m and for
   leeward situations, C alpha (aU(2) + bV(2))(-1/2) (a is a function of
   street geometry, b depends on the characteristics of the vehicles and
   traffic density, V is the average vehicle speed). We obtained empirical
   expressions for b, for C/C-0 (C-0 is the concentration `without' the
   influence of the TPT) and for a critical wind speed (U-C) (which does
   aU(C)(2) = bV(2)). The ratio C/C-0 is 0.71 when U=U-C, not depending on
   the traffic flow.},
