Organization = {Int Assoc Engn Geol \& Environm},
Abstract = {The coastal cliffs of Scarborough, UK which are approximately 5km in
   length, were protected by seawalls around 100 years ago. However, they
   continue to be affected by a range of landslide problems, most notably
   the: recent Holbeck hall landslide in 1993 which led to the destruction
   of a large hotel.. This paper describes how a combination of
   geomorphological mapping, structural inspection and historical records
   have provided a preliminary indication of the landslide risk on the
   Scarborough urban coastline, UK.},
