Note = {19th International Congress on Energy and the Environment, Opatija,
   CROATIA, 2004},
Abstract = {A solution for pollution caused by vehicles is proposed. In particular
   we supply the strategic paths that should be followed in order to
   consider the numerous factors involved in such problem. Starting front
   the problem connected to the fuel production and distribution, we
   describe an integrate technological approach for the choice of the best
   engine that have to be used with relation to the geographical area and
   typology of transport. The material used in the production of vehicles
   have been recognized as an important point to be studied. Ultimately,
   all kind of normative, some time encouraging and some other time
   restrictive, are ``drivers{''} on the road of environmental protection
   in transport. The topics outlined are applied to a specific real urban
   and extra-urban context where the previous proposal can be quantified.
   The availability of resources, the environmental impact of production,
   distribution and combustion of fuel, the technological support are the
   integrated factor making possible more that? one choice. Fuel cells
   alimented by hydrogen are the desirable optimal solution that have a
   minimum realization time of some decade. Now it's necessary a
   transitional strategy that must establish good basis for the achievement
   of the final result. The binomial fuel cycle ``well to wheels{''} and
   the vehicle cycle ``tank to wheels{''}, weighting at the same time the
   pollutant emission and energetic efficiency, suggest different solutions
   with more than one alternative for fuels and engines.- the simultaneous
   convenience of different complementary fuels solutions suggest the
   adoption of a bi-fuel engine; the natural gas is a useful propeller for
   inner combustion engines and a good transient fuel to hydrogen with wide
   availability and low price; is advantageous to introduce the hybrid
   engine for both energetic efficiency and low emission reason. In this
   context of new vehicle production and new fuel supply is essential to
   build an efficient system for the production and distribution of
   hydrogen and natural gas supporting that one existing for the gasoline
   and diesel. Finally, all the deductions are justified by reliable source
   and the proposals are quantified in the actual case of Lombardia.},
