   26-30, 1998},
Organization = {US DHHS, Agcy Tox Subst Dis Registry; NCI, Occupat Epidemiol Brach;
   NIEHS, Superfund Bas Res Program; Pan Amer Hlth Org; Univ Amer Puebla;
   World Meteorol Org},
Abstract = {This study shows the behavior of domestic solid waste in an urban
   community at the border across Mexicali, Baja California, and Calexico,
   California. The behavior and habits of the population are related to the
   ecological conscience of the residents and domestic solid waste
   generation. We consider that people have fallen in a consumption and
   indifference game, believing that the responsibility of what most be
   done with domestic solid waste corresponds to municipal authorities.
   Citizens are not conscious about the impact on the environment of their
   waste discharges. Ignorance about the correct management of domestic
   solid waste makes it necessary to transform every member of the
   community responsible of this matter.},
