Abstract = {The utilization of underground space has provided viable solutions with
   regards to many serious problems that modem cities are faced with.
   Underground development releases valuable space on the surface, improves
   the environmental quality and preserves the city-scape and the
   landscape. Lately, interest in underground space utilization in Greece
   is more intense than ever. This paper presents two characteristic cases
   from Greece's experience. Furthermore, important issues such as the
   public's considerations and land ownership are discussed.},
