   Natl Sci Fdn, Climate Dynam Program},
Abstract = {Recent dendrochronological studies carried out in Besancon are based on
   timbers from 12 inland archaeological sites and 12 shipwrecks all
   located in the French Mediterranean area. Timbers from inland sites have
   become available with the development of urban rescue archaeology in
   French Mediterranean cities and timbers from shipwrecks were collected
   while reopening ancient sites that had been previously excavated. So
   far, 38 mean site chronologies, involving 12 tree species from the
   mesomediterranean, supramediterranean, and subalpine vegetation stages,
   have been built. The current status of these chronologies reflects the
   main difficulties inherent in tree-ring dating in that area, most of
   them due to the scarcity of long-lived tree species, the large number of
   tree species resulting from the arboreal diversity, the importation of
   timber, and the idiosyncrasy of the local climate.},
