Pages = {398-402},
Note = {International Symposium on Environmental Science and Technology,
   Beijing, PEOPLES R CHINA, NOV 13-16, 2007},
Organization = {Chinese Soc Environm Sci; Beijing Inst Technol},
Abstract = {To investigate influences of urbanization process on soil environment,
   the study was conducted in the suburb of Zhengzhou city. The
   concentration of heavy metals Cd, Hg, Pb, As and Cr in the topsoil
   samples were analysis, and the soil environmental quality on the base of
   the environmental background value criteria were evaluated by
   single-factor pollution index and Nemerow multi-factor pollution index
   method respectively. Furthermore, the spatial variability of soil
   pollution in terms of heavy metals was researched with Kriging
   interpolation method. The analytical results indicate that the
   contaminate degree of soil heavy metals has the feature of Cr> Pb> Cd>
   Hg> As, the average contents of heavy metals (Cr, Pb) in the soil exceed
   the backg round values, in which, the concentrations of Cr is higher
   than background value, suggesting that Cr might be considered as a
   dominant element causing soil heavy meta pollution in the study area; Pb
   is in slightly polluted, while other heavy metals are in not polluted
   states; and the synthetic pollution index of all sample have exceed 1,
   so the soil environmental quality are in polluted grades; Regional
   differences of index of soil heavy metal were very notable. The
   expanding of urban could have the strong influence on Cr, have certain
   influence on As, and for other heavy have few influence. This indicated
   that the heavy metals in the rapid urbanization area have been
   influenced by anthropogenic activities, so it could provide a credible
   groundwork to protect cultivated land and realize the sustainable use of
   soil resources.},
