   Water; Entec Europe Ltd; NIREX UK Ltd; Environm Agcy},
Abstract = {A review of contaminated land remediations undertaken at 87 sites on the
   Yorkshire Carboniferous ``Coal Measures{''} aquifer is presented. The
   area contains a widespread legacy of contaminated land that is underlain
   by an aquifer of limited intrinsic resource value. The review leads on
   to discuss what degree of remediation is justified in environments such
   as the Yorkshire Coal Measures and provides a summary of issues that
   influence this question. Due to the widely different local sensitivities
   of sites, the authors advocate the need for site specific
   ``source-pathway-receptor{''} assessments to reliably determine the
   necessary degree of remediation.},
