Abstract = {Unsatisfactory Occupational Safety \& Health (OSH) in the construction
   industry has turned out to be an issue as it contributes to numbers of
   incidents and fatality to the construction players and public. Previous
   research suggested that early introduction of safety \& health elements
   within the project implementation contributed towards minimising this
   issue. Hence, the objective of this paper is to identify the
