Note = {International Workshop on Intelligent Information Technology (2WINTECH),
   Cheonan, SOUTH KOREA, OCT 20-22, 2016},
Abstract = {Saminist or Sedulur Sikep is an indigenous people or local community at
   Kendeng Mountains Sukolilo, Pati. Sedulur Sikep community expected North
   Kendeng Mountains maintained and conserved continuity to be able to
   contribute to the local community whom majority earned living as
   traditional farmers. Sedulur Sikep concerned to the destruction of North
   Kendeng Mountains caused of illegal mining and illegal logging which
   effected directly to local community such as flood, landslide and others
   disaster. This paper aim to analyze the Sedulur Sikep's environmental
   wisdom to conserve North Kendeng Mountain from destruction of illegal
   logging, illegal mining and the plans of construction of a cement
   industries in the North Kendeng Mountains region in Sukolilo, Kayen and
   Tambakromo. This study is the descriptive qualitative research, the data
   in this study were obtained from observation, in-depth interviews,
   discussions, and data reports. The results of this study show that
   environmental wisdom of Sedulur Sikep means of living harmony to North
   Kendeng Mountain. Sedulur Sikep have been having environmental wisdom
   which able to reject the constructing a cement industries in North
   Kendeng Mountain. The success of Sedulur Sikep conserved Kendeng
   Mountains supported by the holding firm of their environmental wisdom
   means living harmony to nature around.},
