Pages = {477-482},
Note = {International Symposium on Safety Science and Technology, Beijing,
   PEOPLES R CHINA, SEP 24-27, 2008},
Abstract = {Only assessing the safety of stand evacuation is not enough for the
   safety of the entire stadium evacuation. In accordance with stands -
   concourse levels-stairs-ground evacuation routines, concourse level also
   plays an important role in stadium evacuation, so we simulate the
   concourse level evacuation with buildingEXODUS. Congestion on concourse
   level and the influence of congestion on evacuation of stand exit are
   investigated and measured. Under the affection of the congestion, the
   total evacuation time of the stand will even exceed the code limit, 8
   minutes. The causes of the congestion include human's preference for
   nearest routine, flow rate of the stands, location of the facade stairs
   and the distance between the inlet and outlet of the concourse. And a
   solution was advocated to lease the congestion in the completed stadium.
   Simulation result shows that flow diversion is a feasible way to
   eliminate the impact of congestion on stand evacuation.},
