   04-08, 1996},
Organization = {Amer Stat Assoc, Sect Stat \& Environm},
Abstract = {A model is proposed for the diurnal behavior of ozone. This diurnal
   model focuses on the dynamics of ozone behavior over the day. By
   identifying the timing and dynamics of the fluctuation as well as the
   general strength of the daily ozone, the model retains far more
   information than commonly used daily summaries. This modeling adds a new
   dimension to the study of ozone and the results can be used as the bases
   for future studies. The model is applied to urban ozone data from
   Houston.},
