   International-Society-for-Brain-Electromagnetic-Topography, Tokyo,
   JAPAN, APR 11-14, 2004},
Organization = {Int Soc Brain Electromagnet Topog},
Abstract = {In order to clarify the brain mechanisms of visual cognition for moving
   objects, evoked cortical magnetic responses for horizontally moving
   object were measured. A major response at the latency around 140 ms
   appeared in the location from the right parietal region. Another
   distinctive response around 240 ms was observed in the right temporal
   region. The neural activity of the dorsal system in the right hemisphere
   was suggested to be necessary to visually catch the moving object and
   recognize it distinctively. (C) 2004 Elsevier B.V. All rights reserved.},
