Abstract = {The most common unethical conduct evidenced by the contractors are cover
   pricing, bid cutting, poor documentation, late and short payments,
   subcontractors' lack of safety ethics, unfair treatment of contractors
   in tender/final account negotiations, competitors' overstatement of
   capacity and qualifications to secure work, competitors' falsification
   of experience and qualifications and bureaucratic, government policy. To
   minimise the lapse of ethical issues in the industry, the suggested
   solutions are divided into short, medium and long term categories based
   on the project time frame. The findings provide useful information to
   stakeholders on how to deal with the pressing ethical issues confronting
   the Malaysian construction industry. (C) 2012 Published by Elsevier B.V.
