Abstract = {3-dimension statistical method is used to simulate the popular
   micro-cell propagation model: COST231-Walfish-Ikegami model{[}6]{[}7].
   The extended model allows for improved path loss estimation by
   consideration the character of the urban environment parameters are
   lognormal random variables rather than deterministic. The numerical
   calculation results and trial measurement data is presented. Based on
   the measurement and modelling results, we find that the 3D COST231-WI
   model fits very well with the measurement result in the metropolitan
   scenario. The conclusion is useful and helpful to network planning in
   the future. (C) 2011 Published by Elsevier Ltd. Selection and/or
