Abstract = {Accounting for the government's intention towards sustainable energy
   development and the deployment of Malaysia's first smart grid system,
   inclusive participation of residential units will transform their role
   from consumers to prosumers, enabling them to become ``positive
   nodes{''} of the smart grid system. This paper evaluates the simulation
   output of a grid displaced electricity demand of a significant
   terrace-based housing cohort in Malaysia. Utilising Integrated
   Environmental Solution Virtual Environment (IESVE) as the simulation
   tool, solar panel retrofitted to the existing terrace houses in urban
   centres across peninsular Malaysia is investigated in order to identify
   its potential to displace current grid electricity demand, consequently
   shaving peak demand and reduced household's `s electricity bill.},
