Abstract = {This study assessed the accessibility of three public buildings of
   tourist attraction in Malaysia; Berjaya Times Square, Museum of History
   and Ethnography Malacca (Stadthuys), and Central Market Kuala Lumpur.
   With the Malaysian government promotion of a caring society, buildings
   of tourist attraction should be accessible to the person with
   disabilities (PWD). Both exterior and interior spaces of these buildings
   should be able to cater the need of PWDs. Site observation, facilities
   simulation done by PWDs, and interviews were conducted to assess the
   buildings' accessibility. From the findings, buildings that have been
   built earlier are less accessible than the newer buildings. (C) 2012
