Note = {3rd All-Russia Population Seminar on Ontogeny and Population, ISOHKAR
   OLA, RUSSIA, FEB 07-11, 2000},
Organization = {Mari State Univ, Dept Botany Ecol Phytophys},
Abstract = {With regard to the concept of a discrete approach to the description of
   seed plant ontogeny, proposed by T.A. Rabotnov and A.A. Uranov, the
   ontogeny of apothecial foliose lichen Xanthoria parietina is described.
   Four periods and 13 ontogenetic states are distinguished by
   morphological and anatomical characters. In the urban environment, the
   thalli of X. parietina perish at early developmental stages (incomplete
   ontogeny); in general, their size and the number and size of apothecia
   decrease and the connection with substrates at the final ontogenetic
   stages becomes weaker. Adaptation of the X. parietina population to
   existence under adverse natural and anthropogenic conditions manifests
   itself in the retarded development of pregenerative individuals and
   elimination of the least tolerant generative individuals.},
