   Inst Architects; Hong Kong Institut Engineers; Hong Kong Inst Surveyors;
   HKSTS; IUE; JSCE; RICS; Urban Planning Soc China; China Civil Engn Soc;
   Hong Kong Inst Util Specialists},
Abstract = {Urbanization in 20th century has destroyed environmental resources and
   wild lives instead of retaining our safe and comfortable lives, and
   concrete structures have contributed to shaping urban spaces as our
   living equipments. These, built on the ground after removing
   environmental resources, seemingly put huge impacts on environment,
   however, concrete structures are only techniques to construct most of
   all infrastructures, that we need, with sustainable costs and
   construction periods. We are now required to use concrete structures
   with more environmental ways. The purpose of the research is to compare
   performance of ready-mixed concrete and pre-cast concrete in aspect of
   CO2 emission and find the optimal demand balance of ready-mixed concrete
   and pre-cast concrete introduced in Tokyo metropolitan area through the
   regional resource flow simulation system named ecoMA. This can evaluate
   not only CO2 emission in production but in transportation, therefore,
   total CO2 emission in an industry are comprehensively evaluated and
   contributes to awareness of the optimal material balance. Conclusively,
   total CO2 emission required in pre-cast concretes are always more than
   that of ready-mixed concrete because energy consumption cannot defeat
   CO2 reduction by saving unit cement volume. The energy saving
   improvement in curing process will be indispensable in the near future.},
