   18-19, 2015},
Organization = {Univ Minho, Sch Engn; Univ Porto, Sch Econ \& Management},
Abstract = {This article outlines problems related to the location of facilities
   designed to treat the organic fraction of municipal solid waste (OFMSW).
   An anaerobic digestion (AD) facility is investigated as a treatment
   option, while taking into account the aspects of energy production to be
   classified as a renewable energy source (Whiting and Azapagic, 2014).
   The use of waste for energy relates to both waste management and energy
   generation issues, this relationship spurred on this research. The
   analysis was focused on urban areas, mainly medium and large cities. One
   of the most difficult issues associated with the sitting of a waste
   processing plant, is its integration with the local infrastructure,
   avoiding conflicts, and negative environmental impacts at the same time.
   This research aims to analyse the possibilities for the location of AD
   plants for OFMSW in Poland. Based on experience of other countries and
   lessons learnt from the analysis of existing facilities in Europe,
   conditions for the location of this type of waste treatment plants were
   defined, with the emphasis on economic, environmental and social
   aspects. Apparently the results of the multicriteria decision analysis
   tool for the sitting of municipal solid waste fermentation plants
   (M-BIST) project could be transferred to other countries, especially
   those with a comparable GDP level and a similar framework for a waste
   management system.},
