Note = {International Conference on Biotechnology, Agriculture, Environment and
   Energy (ICBAEE), Beijing, PEOPLES R CHINA, MAY 22-23, 2014},
Abstract = {The schrebergarten in China emerged in the 1990s, after years of
   development, and in some cities in our country have become a project in
   which many citizens actively participate in the experience. With the
   experience of agriculture development, governments at all levels are
   paying more and more attention to the development of the schrebergarten,
   and many places will develop this kind of experience of agriculture,
   developing the schrebergarten as a means of raising farmers' income and
   improving the rural landscape. In view of the present development
   situation, how to choose a scientific and rational plantation
   development mode, what kind of development mode can better promote the
   healthy development of economy and society, are becoming the key
   questions in the development of schrebergarten. This paper based on the
   experience of agricultural development mode, draws lessons from the
   Japanese schrebergarten development pattern and successful experience,
   and provides theoretical guidance to the health of the experience of
   agriculture development, providing plantations development practices can
   reference the model, so as to promote the rapid development of the rural
   economic and social development and urban and rural integration.},
