Note = {10th International Coastal Symposium (ICS 2009), Lisbon, PORTUGAL, APR
   13-18, 2009},
Organization = {Coastal Educ Res Fdn; Ctr Estud Geograf Planeament Reg; Univ Nova
   Lisbon, Fac Cienc Soc Humanas},
Abstract = {Coastal dunes occur in restrict areas along Rio de Janeiro Coast. These
   environments have been Subjected to a wide variety of investigations
   over the time, using different approaches and issues. In this research
   we mapped three sites of transgressive coastal dunes, identified along
   Rio de Janeiro state, including morphodynamics aspects, occupation and
   implications for the coastal management. Different types of foredunes
   were identified along the Paraiba do Sul delta. The main mechanism for
   dune development is associated with erosional and depositional phases of
   coastline, participating the sedimentary budget between beaches,
   shoreface and fluvial inputs that promotes fort-nation of two types of
   foredunes. The transgressive evolution of foredunes southward to Paraiba
   do Sul river mouth promoting severe erosion along Atafona beach that
   affects buildings and the urban structure. Other area is located between
   Cabo Frio and Cabo Buzios, where the coastal plain is characterized by a
   complex of foredunes, barchans and parabolic dunes. The dynamics of this
   complex system is govern by northeast trade winds. The main coastal
   problem identified in Cabo Frio region is associated to planning new
   resorts and urban structure above the dunes. We concluded that the
   occupation of these areas with no criteria of coastal management and
   respect for Brazilian laws promotes critic conflicts.},
