Abstract = {This study of how the atmospheric stimuli of stores can affect human
   behavior (of customers and employees) was divided into two stages. In
   the first stage, an exploratory research design was used to identify the
   attributes of the exogenous variables, namely the store exterior, store
   interior, interior layout, interior displays and human variables. The
   attributes obtained were then used to conduct the second stage of study
   using path analysis. The effect of the store on the behavior of
   customers was determined by the general interior and interior display,
   while the behavior of the employees was determined by the interior, the
