   Planning and Economics (CEMEPE) /
   International-Society-for-Ecotoxicology-and-Environmental-Safety
   (SECOTOX) Conference, GREECE, JUN 19-24, 2011},
Organization = {Int Soc Ecotoxicol \& Environm Safety; Univ Thessaly, Dept Planning \&
   Reg Dev; Aristotle Univ Thessaloniki, Dept Mech Engn; Natl Tech Univ
   Athens, Sch Mech Engn, Sect Ind Management \& Operat Res; TEI W
   Macedonia, Dept Pollut Control Technologies},
Abstract = {During the last years much research has taken place about urban heat
   island (UHI) effects, mainly concentrated in big cities with an extended
   gap for the smaller. The aim of the paper is to present the analysis
   results of an urban heat island research taking place in a small city of
   Western Greece, Agrinio. The specific research target was to validate
   the presence of the UBI, measure its intensity and determine the
   parameters that correlate with the appearance of the UHI. A network of
   air temperature sensors was developed in 8 different places in the city
   and measurements were recorded every 10 minutes for a period of 6
   months. Data from a meteorological station were also collected for the
   same period. Results show that the city of Agrinio presents strong UHI
   intensities during the night with high values up to 6 degrees C and a
   mean of 3.82 degrees C. During the daytime, cool island effect is also
   observed for about 35\% of day duration. Temperature differences appear
   to be strongly correlated with the dominating wind speed in the city
   since air plays an important role in urban ventilation and creates more
   homogeneous temperatures in urban spar.},
