   Sci Inst Regional Studies},
Abstract = {Comparison of total contents of Ba, Cr, Cu, Mn, Mo, Ni, Sn, Pb, V, Zn,
   Al, Ca, Fe, Mg determined in topsoil of central part of Vilnius by
   optical atomic emission spectrophotometry (OAES) with respective
   contents determined by energy-dispersive x-ray fluorescence (EDXRF),
   analysis of their correlation and linear relationship with and without
   outliers are the tasks of research. For most elements, except Ca, Sn,
   Ba, the contents determined by EDXRF are significantly lower and less
   variable. They can be predicted according to OAES-contents using linear
   equations. After elimination of outliers for all elements the
   correlation is significant at p<0.05.},
